From b15fd68d4145c031b485d8a6edb5202b0a6b250d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:16:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Select V8 stack assembly by Windows ABI

Restore the original MASM source and give the Windows GNU implementation
its own preprocessed assembly file. Select the source with the configured
Windows ABI and declare the existing LLVM constraint dependency in V8.

Issue: https://github.com/holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed/issues/61
Base: rust-v0.162.1 (092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d),
with the preceding downstream build-repair queue.

Red: bazel test --test_output=errors --test_verbose_timeout_warnings
//tools/build-warnings/v8-assembly:all exits 3: GNU analysis selects
push_registers_masm.asm instead of push_registers_gas.S. The original
native Windows job 116473691446 fails when ml64 assembles GNU syntax.

Green: both ABI-selection regressions pass, and bazel build
--platforms=//:windows_x86_64_gnullvm
@v8//:codex_windows_stack_assembly_library_icu compiles the actual GNU
assembly. Maintained just fmt-check and just bazel-lock-check pass.
Native MSVC compilation and Windows runtime acceptance remain required.
